n {R}^{2},$  and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{R}^{2}}g(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{D}g(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}1\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[y]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function $h$ is *not* a valid probability density function because it does not satisfy the first condition. For example,\n\n$$\nh(0,2)=\\frac{0-2}{6}=-\\frac{1}{3}≱0.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$f$ and $g$ only.\"" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346249 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346250 13194139535370 true] [17592186346249 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346251 13194139535370 true] [17592186346249 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346252 13194139535370 true] [17592186346249 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346253 13194139535370 true] [17592186346249 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346254 13194139535370 true] [17592186346249 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535370 true] [17592186346249 1041 "selection" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346249 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346250 13194139535370 true] [17592186346249 1110 #uuid "3017f8be-9b1b-512e-af57-df5318abf3aa" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346250 1034 "$f$ and $g$ only" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346250 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535370 true] [17592186346250 1111 #uuid "d855dda0-1832-54f3-b5fc-b49ed6097c80" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346251 1034 "$g$ only" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346251 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535370 true] [17592186346251 1111 #uuid "ac2baaa1-d256-57c1-b9b8-3ccaa249e88b" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346252 1034 "$g$ and $h$ only" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346252 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535370 true] [17592186346252 1111 #uuid "64549d8e-0810-5f37-902d-0e1867f455f6" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346253 1034 "$f$ only" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346253 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535370 true] [17592186346253 1111 #uuid "3fc6c4b4-549b-5687-986d-ce9b99e3a5b6" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346254 1034 "$f$ and $h$ only" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346254 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535370 true] [17592186346254 1111 #uuid "74c21183-a94b-5f13-bdba-d3f7b89e2204" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346255 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346256 13194139535370 true] [17592186346255 1089 "q-110865" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346255 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535370 true] [17592186346255 1100 "Let $D=[0,2]\\times [0,1].$ Which of the following functions are valid joint probability density functions?\n\n- $f(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2},\\, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}$\n- $g(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}x-y,\\, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}$\n- $h(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}xy,\\, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}$" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346255 1113 #uuid "ffd90769-db03-5a84-9839-38f6442c5a87" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346255 1145 "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- ${∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1$\n\nLet's check the above conditions for each of the given functions.\n\n- The function $f$ is *not* a valid probability density function because it does not satisfy the second condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[3x{y}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[2{y}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2 \\\\  & \\ne 1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function $g$ is *not* a valid probability density function because it does not satisfy the first condition. For example,\n\n$$\ng(0,1)=0-1=-1≱0.\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The function $h$ is a valid probability density function. Indeed, we have $h(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2},$  and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{R}^{2}}h(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{D}h(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}xy\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}xy\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\cdot y]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$h$ only.\"" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346256 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346257 13194139535370 true] [17592186346256 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346258 13194139535370 true] [17592186346256 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346259 13194139535370 true] [17592186346256 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346260 13194139535370 true] [17592186346256 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346261 13194139535370 true] [17592186346256 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535370 true] [17592186346256 1041 "selection" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346256 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346257 13194139535370 true] [17592186346256 1110 #uuid "8f112021-2a00-5cbb-b61a-d38df35ef7f2" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346257 1034 "$h$ only" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346257 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535370 true] [17592186346257 1111 #uuid "51dc79cc-c2d6-50ee-bdcc-aa1eee7a9b86" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346258 1034 "$g$ only" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346258 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535370 true] [17592186346258 1111 #uuid "bcdf2e30-e13d-5c81-84ec-063b0ed08d4c" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346259 1034 "$g$ and $h$ only" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346259 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535370 true] [17592186346259 1111 #uuid "5aae3cfb-3787-5d5a-a14d-8c040b49edf5" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346260 1034 "$f,$ $g,$ and $h$" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346260 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535370 true] [17592186346260 1111 #uuid "164cfb7d-c0d3-59d5-8786-d7eba5b7d60d" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346261 1034 "$f$ only" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346261 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535370 true] [17592186346261 1111 #uuid "5b8b81d9-2ee8-577f-abf8-fd33080cec08" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346262 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346263 13194139535370 true] [17592186346262 1089 "q-110868" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346262 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535370 true] [17592186346262 1100 "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}c\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y),\\, & 0\\le y\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $c$ is a positive real number. Find the value of $c.$" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346262 1113 #uuid "f8890e3b-d9f0-5edf-8858-b6864ec3a81c" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346262 1145 "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- ${∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/a49e679b3919594edc7fe963190a754324b9b5ea980d1936121c040d0ee52284.png)\n\nNow, let's check our conditions:\n\n- Since $c>0,$ we clearly have $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ So the first condition is satisfied.\n\n- For the second condition to be satisfied, we must have \n\n$$\n{∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}c\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nW\nWe evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating  $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}c\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{[-c\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-c\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+c\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(c\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-c\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={[c\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\frac{c\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{2}]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =c\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\frac{c\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )}{2} \\\\  & =c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nc=1.\n$$" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346263 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346264 13194139535370 true] [17592186346263 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346265 13194139535370 true] [17592186346263 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346266 13194139535370 true] [17592186346263 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346267 13194139535370 true] [17592186346263 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346268 13194139535370 true] [17592186346263 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535370 true] [17592186346263 1041 "selection" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346263 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346267 13194139535370 true] [17592186346263 1110 #uuid "f9fd94a9-f00c-5b19-8e86-4e6c811991b4" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346264 1034 "3" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346264 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346264 1111 #uuid "feb721c9-f6aa-5036-9268-8d211fed143a" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346265 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346265 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346265 1111 #uuid "641f6abf-13c9-55f1-80ab-517f544afec9" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346266 1034 "2" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346266 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346266 1111 #uuid "7ddb0b2a-ff3f-5a75-9784-1c07d72a70aa" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346267 1034 "1" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346267 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346267 1111 #uuid "0dcce90f-9727-5493-b402-5e32257e78d7" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346268 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346268 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346268 1111 #uuid "ca8d5bab-89a6-5916-a4fc-95cf72781446" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346269 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346270 13194139535370 true] [17592186346269 1089 "q-110985" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346269 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535370 true] [17592186346269 1100 "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}c(1-xy),\\, & {y}^{2}\\le x\\le y, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhere $c$ is a positive real number. Find the value of $c.$" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346269 1113 #uuid "0936abbb-9e50-567c-890d-40631da84483" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346269 1145 "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- ${∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,{y}^{2}\\le x\\le y}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/1ef0c7b289e24a98366c64b9a213c4f67d2fc63157b3319f0118eb16c514097e.png)\n\nNow, let's check our conditions:\n\n- Since $c>0,$ we clearly have $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ So the first condition is satisfied.\n\n- For the second condition to be satisfied, we must have \n\n$$\n{∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y}c(1-xy)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=1.\n$$\n\nWe evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating  $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y}c(1-xy)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[cx-\\frac{cy{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x={y}^{2}}^{x=y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}c(y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{2}-({y}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{5}}{2}))\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}c(y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{2}-{y}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{5}}{2})\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}c(y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{2}-{y}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{5}}{2})\\,dy & =c{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{4}}{8}-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{6}}{12}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{c}{2}-\\frac{c}{8}-\\frac{c}{3}+\\frac{c}{12}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{c}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{c}{8}=1\\,⇒\\,c=8.\n$$" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346271 13194139535370 true] [17592186346270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346272 13194139535370 true] [17592186346270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346273 13194139535370 true] [17592186346270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346274 13194139535370 true] [17592186346270 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346275 13194139535370 true] [17592186346270 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535370 true] [17592186346270 1041 "selection" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346270 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346273 13194139535370 true] [17592186346270 1110 #uuid "b5fe3691-1723-5a5c-8d1e-b7506d0e0249" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346271 1034 "12" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346271 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346271 1111 #uuid "a708adde-bd6b-52a1-9f62-e622df87e411" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346272 1034 "\\frac{1}{8}" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346272 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346272 1111 #uuid "d4306db3-86b1-5a7e-a5b5-042ff9ada147" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346273 1034 "8" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346273 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346273 1111 #uuid "ec1417ee-51dc-5a94-8125-0d178934c10b" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346274 1034 "\\frac{1}{12}" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346274 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346274 1111 #uuid "76fbf73e-36cb-55ba-b6b0-cce8a0e64238" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346275 1034 "1" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346275 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346275 1111 #uuid "ef682d15-9356-56f8-9b5e-fb3bc7b79e9c" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346276 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346277 13194139535370 true] [17592186346276 1089 "q-110986" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346276 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535370 true] [17592186346276 1100 "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{c}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y},\\, & 1\\le x\\le e,\\,e\\le y\\le {e}^{x}, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhere $c$ is a positive real number. Find the value of $c.$" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346276 1113 #uuid "86d22edc-bcdf-5bbd-9aca-23ca6a278347" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346276 1145 "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- ${∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le e,\\,e\\le y\\le {e}^{x}}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/268e469b0306d22e6b6dc05905a9d56a1cabd4b0e405f741ff458ca241440d4a.png)\n\nNow, let's check our conditions:\n\n- Since $c>0,$ we clearly have $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ So the first condition is satisfied.\n\n- For the second condition to be satisfied, we must have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\frac{c}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dy\\,dx=1.\n$$\n\n$$\n{∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\frac{c}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nWe evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating  $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\frac{c}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{c}{x}[{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\frac{1}{y\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{c}{x}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)]_{y=e}^{y={e}^{x}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{c}{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{x})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e))\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{c\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{c\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}dx & ={[\\frac{c{ln}^{2}⁡x}{2}]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{c{ln}^{2}⁡e}{2}-\\frac{c{ln}^{2}⁡1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{c}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{c}{2}=1\\,⇒\\,c=2.\n$$" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346278 13194139535370 true] [17592186346277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346279 13194139535370 true] [17592186346277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346280 13194139535370 true] [17592186346277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346281 13194139535370 true] [17592186346277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346282 13194139535370 true] [17592186346277 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535370 true] [17592186346277 1041 "selection" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346277 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346279 13194139535370 true] [17592186346277 1110 #uuid "d84369d4-8ad0-581d-af0c-bf33c588aa07" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346278 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346278 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346278 1111 #uuid "3ce47bd2-d131-57c5-9920-86fc56d7b67a" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346279 1034 "2" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346279 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346279 1111 #uuid "cc27a050-cb0f-5a7c-a98f-f849a38f9b01" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346280 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346280 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346280 1111 #uuid "88ad20ec-8a48-5821-9c61-28fecb88e386" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346281 1034 "1" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346281 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346281 1111 #uuid "628c13fb-158f-577f-8098-bb8cdbd706ed" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346282 1034 "4" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346282 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346282 1111 #uuid "8890274b-e436-55ab-9e10-c911c0ce5a24" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346283 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346284 13194139535370 true] [17592186346283 1089 "q-110987" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346283 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535370 true] [17592186346283 1100 "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}cx{e}^{y},\\, & 1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡x, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhere $c$ is a positive real number. Find the value of $c.$" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346283 1113 #uuid "ebb42d17-0dc1-5df4-b258-bdc2fae854db" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346283 1145 "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- ${∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/8a94024cbce0389b1d9c60bf64a38cb7c8e8e52836b2b39e9e638f856a1c5269.png)\n\nNow, let's check our conditions:\n\n- Since $c>0,$ we clearly have $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ So the first condition is satisfied.\n\n- For the second condition to be satisfied, we must have \n\n$$\n{∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}cx{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nWe evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating  $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}cx{e}^{y}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}cx[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{e}^{y}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}cx[{e}^{y}]_{y=0}^{y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}cx({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}-{e}^{0})dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}cx(x-1)dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(c{x}^{2}-cx)dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(c{x}^{2}-cx)dx & ={[\\frac{c{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{c{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{8c}{3}-\\frac{4c}{2})-(\\frac{c}{3}-\\frac{c}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5c}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{5c}{6}=1\\,⇒\\,c=\\frac{6}{5}.\n$$" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346284 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346285 13194139535370 true] [17592186346284 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346286 13194139535370 true] [17592186346284 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346287 13194139535370 true] [17592186346284 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346288 13194139535370 true] [17592186346284 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346289 13194139535370 true] [17592186346284 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535370 true] [17592186346284 1041 "selection" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346284 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346286 13194139535370 true] [17592186346284 1110 #uuid "5dba9fcb-0c02-5b23-966d-2cd3ae950928" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346285 1034 "\\frac{5}{6}" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346285 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346285 1111 #uuid "50cb7ee5-d867-59a5-bd04-b6654c703374" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346286 1034 "\\frac{6}{5}" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346286 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346286 1111 #uuid "4c9eec72-68d9-541e-86d5-d914b897362b" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346287 1034 "\\frac{3}{5}" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346287 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346287 1111 #uuid "0e504688-fa64-5b33-a8f9-11418206011e" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346288 1034 "1" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346288 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346288 1111 #uuid "1ab3e703-0277-5209-8933-cb51ec37c29c" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346289 1034 "\\frac{5}{3}" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346289 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346289 1111 #uuid "f819e9ff-0b47-50ad-910d-611d3a426d79" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346290 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346291 13194139535370 true] [17592186346290 1089 "q-111150" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346290 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535370 true] [17592186346290 1100 "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{xy}{4},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X<Y).$" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346290 1113 #uuid "15866248-87b8-5440-85e9-a5b2bdb2a1b7" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346290 1145 "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A⊂{R}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nP((X,Y)\\in A)={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D=[0,2]\\times [0,2],$ and the event $A={X<Y}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/9213a4b132f625677fcc5719e71900d037ac08088dc477f8d6a93f9ca67bc3d4.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<Y) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{xy}{4}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{xy}{4}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}y}{8}]}_{x=0}^{x=y}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{{y}^{3}}{8}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{4}}{32}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 131941