& x\\ge 0,\\,y\\ge 0, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X+Y<1).$ Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." 13194139535370 true] [17592186346297 1113 #uuid "58a14ca3-7ee8-5b93-a4bb-5d0edad0644d" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346297 1145 "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A⊂{R}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nP((X,Y)\\in A)={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D=[0,\\infty )\\times [0,\\infty ),$ and the event $A={X+Y<1}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/df0bf32b4785a9f43946bd3b08f1b255549485f2275c74607fb5285e2b1baa3c.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X+Y<1) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-y}{e}^{-x-y}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-y}{e}^{-x-y}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[-{e}^{-x-y}]_{x=0}^{x=1-y}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{-y}-{e}^{-1})\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[-{e}^{-y}-{e}^{-1}y]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-1}-{e}^{-1}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{e-2}{e} \\\\  & ≈0.264.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346298 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346299 13194139535370 true] [17592186346298 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346300 13194139535370 true] [17592186346298 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346301 13194139535370 true] [17592186346298 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346302 13194139535370 true] [17592186346298 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346303 13194139535370 true] [17592186346298 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535370 true] [17592186346298 1041 "selection" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346298 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346303 13194139535370 true] [17592186346298 1110 #uuid "f9ecdac5-8654-5d25-984f-915c9974dfb5" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346299 1034 "0.421" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346299 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346299 1111 #uuid "ea29f6d8-31d0-510e-a564-c5fe83a4a597" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346300 1034 "0.528" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346300 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346300 1111 #uuid "510a0901-b221-5ddd-bc99-0aaca1bb179a" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346301 1034 "0.132" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346301 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346301 1111 #uuid "2802c2c6-4a75-569d-901c-d452b1829484" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346302 1034 "0.375" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346302 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346302 1111 #uuid "9b04e26a-7498-569f-ab4a-0d1d4a5a4ebf" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346303 1034 "0.264" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346303 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346303 1111 #uuid "90f36157-0b2b-5f85-a6cd-981f05711307" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346304 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346305 13194139535370 true] [17592186346304 1089 "q-111163" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346304 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535370 true] [17592186346304 1100 "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{(1+x+y)^{3}},\\, & 0\\le y\\le x, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X+Y<2).$" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346304 1113 #uuid "9d00d275-db06-5f3f-ae74-29e8404f94a4" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346304 1145 "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A⊂{R}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nP((X,Y)\\in A)={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D={0\\le y\\le x},$ and the event $A={X+Y<2}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/f7a0f0fb9d20a4b88d0aa4c395e2adb1d62195601ce756f57a48becc6ab38681.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X+Y<2) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{2-y}\\frac{4}{(1+x+y)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{y}^{2-y}\\frac{4}{(1+x+y)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[-\\frac{2}{(1+x+y)^{2}}]}_{x=y}^{x=2-y}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{2}{(1+2y)^{2}}-\\frac{2}{9})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{1+2y}-\\frac{2y}{9}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{2}{9}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346306 13194139535370 true] [17592186346305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346307 13194139535370 true] [17592186346305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346308 13194139535370 true] [17592186346305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346309 13194139535370 true] [17592186346305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346310 13194139535370 true] [17592186346305 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535370 true] [17592186346305 1041 "selection" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346305 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346307 13194139535370 true] [17592186346305 1110 #uuid "ed563015-d856-5448-bfc8-c5bb1d5eedc3" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346306 1034 "\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346306 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346306 1111 #uuid "37609cdf-d9fe-5671-9c36-cb27c3a2123b" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346307 1034 "\\frac{4}{9}" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346307 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346307 1111 #uuid "71e3af58-e13f-548e-98d9-16143300261b" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346308 1034 "\\frac{2}{9}" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346308 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346308 1111 #uuid "9aee4e20-a13b-59fe-a62b-1da5e771baca" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346309 1034 "\\frac{4}{27}" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346309 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346309 1111 #uuid "f19b1722-22f8-57cf-b8e0-9ecc213abb90" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346310 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346310 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535370 true] [17592186346310 1111 #uuid "ca4ee91d-9521-50b4-b2ce-fa65fa7a62e0" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346311 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346312 13194139535370 true] [17592186346311 1089 "q-111167" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346311 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535370 true] [17592186346311 1100 "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}1,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X+Y>1).$" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346311 1113 #uuid "0ddb1c47-bdc4-5f33-8d84-507752a44afb" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346311 1145 "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A⊂{R}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nP((X,Y)\\in A)={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D=[0,1]\\times [0,1],$ and the event $A={X+Y>1}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/58c1beb1b13680e330260d93fdf8e60460e2bfeae4c1cbbc2fce8b261afe7ea1.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X+Y>1) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{A}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\text{Area}(A) \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346312 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346313 13194139535370 true] [17592186346312 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346314 13194139535370 true] [17592186346312 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346315 13194139535370 true] [17592186346312 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346316 13194139535370 true] [17592186346312 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346317 13194139535370 true] [17592186346312 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535370 true] [17592186346312 1041 "selection" 13194139535370 true] [17592186346